{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCoavc2dE9QSCrDTrmkF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Answer:** O3 wraps the component's dynamic import in a function, so the module is fetched only when the framework asks for its lifecycle. Extensions and modals reach that function through `loadLifeCycles`, and pages reach it through single-spa's `registerApplication`.\n\n**Flow**\n\n1. **Module side:** an app's `index.ts` exports `getAsyncLifecycle(() => import('./x.component'), options)`. The call returns `() => lazy().then(...)`, so nothing is imported until that returned function runs. `getLifecycle` then wraps the component with `singleSpaReact` and `openmrsComponentDecorator`. (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/getLifecycle.ts`)\n2. **Registration side:** `routes.json` entries are registered with a `load` closure, `() => loadLifeCycles(appName, extension.component)` for extensions and modals, and `() => loadLifeCycles(page.appName, page.component)` for pages. Nothing is loaded at registration time.\n3. **Load time:** `loadLifeCycles` calls `importDynamic(appName)`, runs the app's `startupApp()` once (tracked in `initializedApps`), then calls the named export to get the lifecycle. If the app or export is missing, it warns and returns an empty lifecycle. (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-routes/src/loaders/load-lifecycles.ts`)\n\nI did not read the extensions render code, so I have not confirmed exactly when an extension's `load` is invoked. I also did not read `openmrsComponentDecorator`.\n\n**Documentation**\n- `getAsyncLifecycle` reference page, with the lazy-loading description and example.\n- `getSyncLifecycle` page, which contrasts the eager case.\n- The API index entry and the deprecated `getAsyncExtensionLifecycle` alias.\n\n**Usage examples**\n- `esm-devtools-app` and `esm-login-app` export lazy lifecycles from `index.ts`.\n\nNote that `React.lazy` in `esm-implementer-tools-app` is a separate, component-internal mechanism and is not part of the O3 loading path, so I left it out.\n\nDeclarations, best first:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/getLifecycle.ts\", \"startLine\": 52, \"endLine\": 57},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/getLifecycle.ts\", \"startLine\": 26, \"endLine\": 32},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/getLifecycle.ts\", \"startLine\": 77, \"endLine\": 79},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/getLifecycle.ts\", \"startLine\": 84, \"endLine\": 84},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-routes/src/loaders/load-lifecycles.ts\", \"startLine\": 35, \"endLine\": 58},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-routes/src/loaders/load-lifecycles.ts\", \"startLine\": 86, \"endLine\": 109},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-routes/src/loaders/load-lifecycles.ts\", \"startLine\": 60, \"endLine\": 70},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-routes/src/loaders/components.ts\", \"startLine\": 56, \"endLine\": 66},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-routes/src/loaders/components.ts\", \"startLine\": 78, \"endLine\": 104},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-routes/src/loaders/pages.ts\", \"startLine\": 237, \"endLine\": 239},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/getAsyncLifecycle.md\", \"startLine\": 9, \"endLine\": 12},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/getAsyncLifecycle.md\", \"startLine\": 47, \"endLine\": 51},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/getSyncLifecycle.md\", \"startLine\": 10, \"endLine\": 12},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/variables/getAsyncExtensionLifecycle.md\"